      "math_academy_id": "e-4981",
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1, 2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Find a point that must lie on the graph of $y= f(-x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=f(-x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $y$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(1, 2)$ lies $1$ unit to the *right*  of the $y$-axis. So, after the transformation is applied and the point is reflected across the $y$-axis, this point will lie $1$ unit to the *left* of the $y$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the point $P'(-1, 2)$ must lie on the graph of $y=f(-x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224557/assets/0aa23b1c8182d0901e27f9d1df84c30fef44396f6787f370932569f4903fb419.png)",
